From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:49:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 25/52] Create profile: createprofile's first scene and the
 keyboard's frame changes

From the code: createprofile starts with CreateGamerProfile.xur (90105388,
mode 0; GamerTagScene), a half-width scene that shows only its legends and,
once on screen, checks the storage device and shows vk's keyboard (full
width). The HUD adopts each HUD scene's width and legends as it transitions
in (xam 818D4F88: 818D4C10 legends, 818D4C78 state). So:
- the Guide opens half width with that scene (ClosedToHalf), then the frame
  widens for the keyboard (HalfToFull, its A/B legends moving in);
- Back on Save Gamer Profile returns to that scene (FullToHalf) and it shows
  the keyboard again (HalfToFull) with the name;
- keyboard -> Save Gamer Profile stays full width (unchanged).
Also the name error box has the error icon (XamShowMessageBox flags 1).
The Save Gamer Profile panel timelines are one frame long, so their
instant change was already right.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AFb8CDFE1Ms5NnJH88eG8b
